docs/WEBSITE_PLAN.md:122:The owner has granted policies A-D: (A) uniquely and exclusively created, sanitized migration JSON evidence under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\OAF Website\BootstrapAudit\MigrationAudit\`, separate from Stage 4C, with flush and file fsync; (B) retention until separately authorized archival/disposal, with no automatic deletion; (C) distinct deliberate owner-issued, environment/operation/revision/start-state/artifact/prerequisite-bound UTC authorizations, unique and single-use, expiring within 24 hours; and (D) fail-closed denial/audit handling, preservation of acknowledged commits, no uncertain retries, permanent claims, deterministic progression after fully verified success or conclusive safe premutation failure, and exceptional owner reconciliation for uncertain outcomes, postcommit audit failures, or incomplete/contradictory evidence. The exact local record/issuer procedure, durability limits, and same-account security boundary are documented in `WORKFLOW.md` under the Stage 5 entry. These policies are approved and must not be reopened as unresolved policy questions.
docs/WEBSITE_PLAN.md:132:`oaf_website/migration_authority.py` supplies the concrete file adapter and minimum deliberate issuer. The migration CLI consumes an existing authorization UUID; direct runner calls and Alembic enforce the same gate and run binding. Fixed environment claim slots prevent concurrent consumption even across different authorization IDs. All claims remain evidence, including partial writes. Completed issuance and terminal evidence use synchronized pending records and exclusive completion publication, bound to exact authorization/run UUIDs and evidence hashes; residual JSON alone never qualifies. Fully verified success, verified no-op, and conclusive safe premutation failure permit a new separately owner-authorized operation without exceptional reconciliation. Uncertain commits, postcommit audit failures, or incomplete/contradictory evidence require an explicit owner reconciliation attestation bound to the exact predecessor bytes and verified state. Development still requires completed successful testing validation of matching artifacts and its own authorization; reconciliation alone cannot supply that result. Exact authorization validity is rechecked after audit persistence immediately before mutation and commit. The migration connection explicitly requires `require_auth="scram-sha-256"`.
docs/WEBSITE_PLAN.md:244:Initially prohibit nontransactional migration operations, revision-controlled commits, autocommit blocks, ordinary downgrade, stamp, automatic destructive repair, and blind retries after uncertain commits. Authorized administrative intervention remains appropriate for exceptional changes, destructive recovery, ownership corrections, and unexplained drift.
